{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgfhcr9qpzjg5BkAQjM8Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't determine B for this complex, and Dq is only a rough estimate.\n\n**Why B can't be fitted:** Cu(II) is d⁹, which is a single positive hole in the e_g set. Its ground term is ²D, and in an octahedral or tetragonal field the spin-allowed levels depend only on Dq and the tetragonal splittings (Ds, Dt), not on the Racah B. Band positions therefore cannot constrain B, so the ts_fit_spectrum and ts_ratio_fit tools are not applicable here. The tool suite also only covers d²–d⁸, so no d⁹ diagram is available.\n\n**Why Dq is only approximate:** In an ideal octahedron the single d⁹ band is ²E_g ← ²T_2g at 10Dq. Here the axial water ligands cause a Jahn-Teller tetragonal distortion, so the observed band at 14 720 cm⁻¹ is a composite of several components, and the shoulder near 12 240 cm⁻¹ is one of them. Taking the band maximum as roughly 10Dq gives:\n\nDq ≈ 1 470 cm⁻¹\n\nThis is an order-of-magnitude estimate. A proper value would require fitting the tetragonal components (Dq, Ds, Dt), which is beyond the tools available here.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1470, \"B\": null, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": true, \"reason\": \"Dq is only a rough estimate from the band maximum because of Jahn-Teller splitting, and B cannot be determined since d9 spin-allowed levels do not depend on B.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8024,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8024,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4fe20624-e8bc-4b02-bf79-77a41c096ef2","uuid":"e2721a10-fe52-43b6-ab15-b4cf79987deb","timestamp":"